Z||000001||qwikgta||10-08-2001||09:18 PM||||I recently got a chance to see one for the first time at the FOCOA show in Virginia.  It didn't look that hard, if you have the parts and the tools.  It had a FWD Olds trannie in it and used the suspension from the Fiero.  From the struts to the control arms it was all fireo.  A lot of cutting and welding to make the engine sit at the correct place in the bay but again if you have the time and skills it looked do-able.  The big problem was exhaust cause' the axles and suspension parts got in the way of the headers, so he had on diff tube lengh headers and it needed same size tubes.  That was going to be his winter project.<P>Rob<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/455_in_a_fiero.jpg"> <P><BR><P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 66K, Header no Cat w/ Supertrapp, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, GT rear swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents, clear tails, KYB's, dropped springs.<BR>http://www.homestead.com/robsfieroproject/robsfieroproject.html   <BR>http://www.vafieros.com<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
